msgstr "دعم الخدمات"

#. Network form, 'Services support' section, shown to IRC operators: which IRC services package the network runs (e.g. X3) and the nicknames of its bots and channels. Jargon to keep: X3, O3, AuthServ, ChanServ, G-line, oper, snoop. Help text under the bot fields; {package} is the services package's name (X3).
#: client/components/NetworkForm.vue
msgctxt "form.servicesHelp"
msgid "Prefilled with the usual names for {package}; change them if this network renamed its bots. Leave a channel blank if the network doesn't run it."
msgstr "مُعبّأة بالأسماء المعتادة لـ {package}؛ غيّرها إن أعادت هذه الشبكة تسمية بوتاتها. اترك القناة فارغة إن لم تكن الشبكة تشغّلها."

#. Network form, 'Services support' section, shown to IRC operators: which IRC services package the network runs (e.g. X3) and the nicknames of its bots and channels. Jargon to keep: X3, O3, AuthServ, ChanServ, G-line, oper, snoop. The package select's first option: no services support.
#: client/components/NetworkForm.vue
msgctxt "form.servicesNone"
msgid "None"
msgstr "لا شيء"

#. Network form, 'Services support' section, shown to IRC operators: which IRC services package the network runs (e.g. X3) and the nicknames of its bots and channels. Jargon to keep: X3, O3, AuthServ, ChanServ, G-line, oper, snoop. Field label: the nickname of the oper service bot (O3 on X3).
#: client/components/NetworkForm.vue
msgctxt "form.servicesOper"
