msgid "A wildcard host needs at least two dots."
msgstr "يحتاج المضيف ذو أحرف البدل إلى نقطتين على الأقل."

#. Oper tools, ban dialog: error under the mask field when an IPv6 mask contains a wildcard (* or ?), which the server refuses; the oper must write a CIDR range instead (2001:db8::/32 is an example, keep it as is). Keep IRC/oper jargon as is (G-line, shun, Z-line, K-line, oper, X3, O3, AuthServ, ChanServ) and every {placeholder} verbatim.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/nefarious/bans.ts
msgctxt "oper.ban.check.v6Wildcard"
msgid "IPv6 masks cannot use wildcards; use CIDR (e.g. 2001:db8::/32)."
msgstr "لا يمكن لأقنعة IPv6 استخدام أحرف البدل؛ استخدم CIDR (مثل 2001:db8::/32)."

