msgstr "حظر مُعدَّل"

#. A nefarious2 server notice in plain words, shown in chat to an IRC operator (kind ban.modify). Each {placeholder} is filled from the notice and rendered as a nick, chip or plain text: keep every placeholder exactly, reorder freely, and do not inflect around them. Similar length to the English.
#. Placeholders: {oper} is the nick of the oper who did it; {server} is a server name; {type} is the ban type: G-line, K-line, Z-line, shun or 'channel ban' (translated separately); {mask} is a ban mask (a chip); {changes} is the server's own list of changes, verbatim. Only one of the two adjacent placeholders before the verb is ever filled (an oper's nick or a server name): keep them side by side.
#. {type} is the ban's kind as the server names it, in English (G-line, Z-line, Shun, K-line, Jupe); its grammatical gender in your language is unknown and varies, so write no article, adjective or verb ending that has to agree with it: use a neutral frame, e.g. 'ban ({type})' or '{type}:' — in English it reads 'a {type}'.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/noticeText.ts
msgctxt "oper.kind.ban.modify.template"
msgid "{oper}{server} changed the global {type} on {mask}:{changes}"
msgstr "{oper}{server}: عُدِّل الحظر العام ({type}) على {mask}:{changes}"

